• Assessed the governance framework around ECL, including approval and review of models, key assumptions, and management overlays by the Senior Management/Audit Committee in accordance with the Board-approved ECL Policy and documentation supporting provisioning logic.
Under Ind AS 109, “Financial Instruments”, allowance for loan losses is determined using Expected Credit Loss (‘ECL’) estimation model. The ECL framework integrates both model-based outcomes and significant management judgement through overlays.
The estimation of ECL on financial instruments involves significant management judgement and estimates and the use of different modelling techniques and assumptions, which could have a material impact on reported profits and, therefore, increased levels of audit focus in the Company’s estimation of ECLs, which are as under:
• Considered the Company's accounting policies for estimation of Expected Credit Loss on loans and assessing compliance with the policies in terms of Ind AS 109;
• Assessed consistency of accounting policies with those applied in the previous year and obtained an understanding of the Management’s updated processes, systems and controls implemented in relation to impairment allowance process;

